+ L1 A row lands once, by the worker holding its lease, and a lease lost is a session ended.
+ L2 eutropia writes nothing on the remote but its own refs.
+ L3 Same facts, same step, on the claim's commit. Every decision is a pure function of the queue, the unit's state, an event, and durations measured by the caller. A row runs on the queue configuration of the commit it was claimed at.
+ L4 Capacity is a token. A machine claims no row without a free slot, and mints no slot under its disk floor.
+ L5 A person decides what only a person may.
+ L6 An absence is named, never defaulted: a fold gap, an unreadable remote, a chain at a newer schema.
+ L7 Staleness is the observer's: a lease is stale only by its own monotonic clock, from the moment it first saw the lease's tip.
+ L8 A session's only input to the loop is its one result.
+ L9 Every waiting state has an exit that will arrive: a process the loop owns, or a budget.
+ L10 Strikes, continuations and parks live on the row's chain and count across machines; a takeover is not a strike.
+ L11 A row lands only through its repository's own gate: its claim commit's land check, run on the tree that lands, when the queue declares one; and the clone's push hooks unless the queue skips them.

